{"slug":"readme","title":"Barkpark","blocks":[
{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The workspace your AI works in.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Barkpark is a headless CMS built for AI agents: a place where an AI stores, sorts, and structures content — "},{"type":"text","value":"tasks, papers, media","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — while you edit the same documents in a browser Studio. The agent drives the API; you drive the panes; both see every change in real time."}]},
{"id":"b2","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Live demo:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://api.barkpark.cloud/studio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://api.barkpark.cloud/studio"}]}]},
{"id":"b3","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Setup"},
{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"bp","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" CLI:","marks":["strong"]}]},
{"id":"b5","type":"code","value":"# macOS / Linux\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FRIKKern/barkpark/main/scripts/install-cli.sh | sh"},
{"id":"b6","type":"code","value":"# Windows (PowerShell)\nirm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FRIKKern/barkpark/main/scripts/install-cli.ps1 | iex"},
{"id":"b7","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Then "},{"type":"text","value":"bp setup","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (local · deploy · connect) and "},{"type":"text","value":"bp task ready","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},
{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Local server, zero config:","marks":["strong"]}]},
{"id":"b9","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"macOS / Linux:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"bp setup --target local","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (native or "},{"type":"text","value":"--docker","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],
[{"type":"text","value":"Windows:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" clone, then "},{"type":"text","value":".\\scripts\\setup-windows.ps1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — installs the toolchain + starts Phoenix"}]
]},
{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Quickstart · Windows · from source"}]},
{"id":"b11","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Your AI's task board"},
{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Task management is the headline use case. Tasks are plain documents with a lifecycle ("},{"type":"text","value":"open → in_progress → done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", plus "},{"type":"text","value":"blocked","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"cancelled","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), a dependency graph, priorities, labels, and an atomic claim/close contract built for concurrent workers (fencing epochs, 300s lease sweeps):"}]},
{"id":"b13","type":"code","value":"bp task prime --worker a1    # one call: my claims + ready head + events + counts\nbp task next agent-1         # atomically claim the next ready task\nbp task claim t1 a1 --resources lib/x.ex   # fence files against parallel workers\nbp task close t1 agent-1 1   # CAS on the claim epoch"},
{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and the same queue is the "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks ✅","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" pane: you flip lifecycle states and set priority/assignee while the agent claims and closes over HTTP (claims and dependencies render read-only — the API owns them). A root task is a goal; subtasks nest under it via "},{"type":"text","value":"parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Guide: "},{"type":"text","value":"docs/setup/TASK-SYSTEM.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" · cheatsheet: "},{"type":"text","value":"docs/cheatsheets/tasks.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},
{"id":"b15","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Play around without stacking up mess"},
{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"One call spins up a "},{"type":"text","value":"workspace","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — it arrives with you as owner, a Default project, and a production dataset. Experiments live in their own workspace with their own schemas, tasks, papers, and media; when the spike is done, nothing leaks back into your real work:"}]},
{"id":"b17","type":"code","value":"bp workspace create Spike\nbp -w spike workspace project-create agents-v2"},
{"id":"b18","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Four ways in"},
{"id":"b19","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Surface"}],[{"type":"text","value":"What it is"}]],"rows":[
[[{"type":"text","value":"bp CLI","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"One static binary that speaks the whole API — "},{"type":"text","value":"bp <noun> <verb>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", assembled live from "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/capabilities","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Same binary as the TUI."}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"Web Studio","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-pane LiveView desk at "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — drill, filter, edit-with-autosave, publish. Real-time across tabs."}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"Terminal TUI","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"The same desk in your terminal, keyboard-driven ("},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" with no args)."}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"REST API","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Public reads, token-authed writes, Sanity-compatible mutation envelope, SSE change stream."}]]
]},
{"id":"b20","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Stack: Elixir 1.15+ / Phoenix LiveView 1.1 / PostgreSQL / Oban · Go 1.24+ (CLI + TUI, one binary) · Caddy. 2400+ mix tests, 89 HTTP integration tests."}]},
{"id":"b21","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Design philosophy"},
{"id":"b22","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"Built for agents.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"bp capabilities -o json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" teaches the whole API in one call; JSON defaults when piped; atomic batch writes via "},{"type":"text","value":"-f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"text","value":"--dry-run","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" previews; "},{"type":"text","value":"-q","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" minimal receipts; stable exit codes."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"One schema, multiple surfaces.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" A single SchemaDefinition drives the Studio panes, the TUI desk, the REST contract, and the CLI command surface."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"Manifest-driven contract.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" The server projects nouns, verbs, and routes into "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/capabilities","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; every client reads the same projection. Default-deny and existence-hiding, keyed on the caller's auth tier."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"The plugin highway.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Plugins are first-party Elixir modules riding the documented "},{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark.Plugin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" behaviour — schemas, routes, workers, cron, resolvers, desk items, CLI verbs travel from Elixir module to manifest to "},{"type":"text","value":"bp","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" shell with no client code at any hop. "},{"type":"text","value":"With all plugins off, Barkpark still works","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the fresh-install invariant is the test of correctness."}]
]},
{"id":"b23","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundled plugins: "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" board above) · "},{"type":"text","value":"Bulldocs","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (portable-doc papers at "},{"type":"text","value":"/papers/:slug","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") · "},{"type":"text","value":"Media","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (asset library) · "},{"type":"text","value":"OnixEdit","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (ONIX 3.0 book metadata + Bokbasen submission) · "},{"type":"text","value":"Frt","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (Godot game content)."}]},
{"id":"b24","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"v1 scope, honestly"},
{"id":"b25","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"No MCP server yet (deferred); "},{"type":"text","value":"bp login","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"completion","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" are stubs; "},{"type":"text","value":"scoped_prefix","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" has no effect yet; "},{"type":"text","value":"--dry-run","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is a client-side preview. The TUI edits v1 primitive fields natively — v2 plugin types render as JSON there (edit in Studio). Plugins disable, never delete. Ledger: "},{"type":"text","value":"docs/decisions/deferred.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},
{"id":"b26","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Deploy"},
{"id":"b27","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"One command on any Ubuntu 22.04+ box. "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"requires","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"DOMAIN","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the public DNS hostname, never an IP (it pins Phoenix "},{"type":"text","value":"check_origin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},
{"id":"b28","type":"code","value":"DOMAIN=api.barkpark.cloud ssh root@YOUR_VPS_IP \"DOMAIN=$DOMAIN bash -s\" < deploy.sh"},
{"id":"b29","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Or let the wizard drive it: "},{"type":"text","value":"bp setup --target deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Updates: "},{"type":"text","value":"ssh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" in, "},{"type":"text","value":"cd /opt/barkpark && git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (post-merge hook rebuilds + restarts). Ops canon: "},{"type":"text","value":"docs/ops/PROD_OPS.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},
